=== Motor A ===
Driver tmc5160 on stepper_x (motor A), accelerometer beacon, kinematics cartesian, registers {'tbl': 2, 'toff': 3, 'hstrt': 5, 'hend': 2, 'tpfd': 4}
Motor A is a rail of 2 TMC5160 drivers (stepper_x, stepper_x1): one G1 of the head moves them together along X; speeds and accels in belt mm, as on one motor
  head: F1200-7200 for 20-120 mm/s of belt, M204 S2500 for 2500 mm/s2 of belt
  max_velocity 1200 caps the belt at 1200 mm/s
  a curve still rising at the top extends the scan up to 354 mm/s
  moves through the bed center, the longest from X22.6 Y92.2 to X148.4 Y92.2 (G-code coordinates); nearest a bed edge 31.6 mm, at 120 mm/s (kept: X 25, Y 25 mm)
  for the moves: minimum_cruise_ratio 0 -> 0, input shaper (by config X 80 Hz, Y 89.8 Hz) -> off (every homing runs on your own settings)
  stepper_x: registers tbl2_toff3_hstrt5_hend2_tpfd4, spreadCycle; run_current 1.8 A; its own enable pin
  stepper_x1: registers tbl2_toff3_hstrt5_hend2_tpfd4, spreadCycle; run_current 1.8 A; its own enable pin
Every X/Y motor holds under current the whole run: stepper_x its run_current 1.8 A, stepper_x1 its run_current 1.8 A, stepper_y its run_current 1.8 A, stepper_y1 its run_current 1.8 A
